[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Bulwark Webmail has been installed to %%WWWDIR%%.

To start it, enable and start the service:

  # sysrc bulwark_enable=YES
  # service bulwark start

By default it listens on 127.0.0.1:3000 (bulwark_listen, bulwark_port in
rc.conf). Put a TLS-terminating reverse proxy such as nginx in front of it.

Most settings are made in the setup wizard on first launch. Settings can
also be given in %%ETCDIR%%/bulwark.env (see
%%ETCDIR%%/bulwark.env.sample, e.g. JMAP_SERVER_URL). Keep the file
readable for root and the %%GROUP%% group only, as it may hold secrets.

Data (admin configuration, settings sync, plugin secrets) is kept in
/var/db/bulwark, the Next.js cache in /var/cache/bulwark.
EOM
}
]
